  "markdown-basic": {
    "source": "# Notification center redesign\n\nGather scattered notifications in **one place** so important ones like failed payments are *never missed*. The background is in the [design doc](#).\n\n## Goals\n\n1. See failed payments `within a day`\n2. Cut muted notifications to 10%\n   - Promotions off by default\n   - ~~Bundle every notification~~ is out of scope\n\n## To do\n\n- [x] Screen design\n- [ ] Beta\n- [ ] Full launch\n\n> [!WARNING] Decision needed\n> Turning promotions off by default needs marketing sign-off.\n\n| Metric | Now | Goal |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Failed payment seen | 2.4 days | 1 day |\n| Muted | 18% | 10% |\n\n```ts\nconst unread = notifications.filter((n) => !n.read);\n```\n\n---\n\n> Fewer notifications get read more."
  },
  "markdown-editor": {
    "source": "# Weekly retro\n\nWrite what **went well** and what didn't, block by block. Type `- ` and it becomes a list right away, type `/` to pick blocks and UI, and drag a block by its handle.\n\n## Went well\n\n- Notification center beta shipped\n- Failed payments seen in 1.2 days instead of 2.4\n\n## Next week\n\n- [x] Write up the retro\n- [ ] Prepare the staged rollout\n\n> [!NOTE] Note\n> Standard markdown tables are drawn as the design system's table.\n\n| Metric | Last week | This week |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Failed payment seen | 2.4 days | 1.2 days |\n| Muted | 18% | 15% |"
  },
  "markdown-ui": {
    "todaySVisits": "## Today's visits\n\nThe card below is drawn from JSON written in a `ui` code block inside the markdown.\n\n```ui\n{ \"type\": \"Widget\", \"props\": { \"id\": \"visits\", \"title\": \"Visitors\", \"w\": 6, \"h\": 2 },\n  \"children\": { \"type\": \"Stat\", \"props\": { \"value\": { \"$data\": \"visits.today\", \"$format\": \"count\" }, \"delta\": { \"change\": { \"$data\": \"visits.change\" }, \"label\": \"vs yesterday\" } } } }\n```\n\n```ui\n{ \"type\": \"Button\", \"props\": { \"variant\": \"primary\", \"onClick\": { \"$action\": { \"name\": \"open-report\" } } }, \"children\": \"Open report\" }\n```\n\n## Weekly active minutes\n\nA standard `mermaid` chart block draws with the design system's chart components here, and as a Mermaid chart on GitHub.\n\n```mermaid\nxychart-beta\n  title \"Weekly active minutes\"\n  x-axis [W1, W2, W3, W4]\n  y-axis \"min\"\n  bar [260, 290, 285, 410]\n```\n\n```mermaid\npie title Visits by device\n  \"Phone\" : 62\n  \"Desktop\" : 31\n  \"Tablet\" : 7\n```\n"
  },
